{
  "area": "traversal",
  "file": "traversal/vehicles-only",
  "description": "traversal-vehicles in a game that runs the vehicles pack without traversal (PL.core-vehicle-rules, U106(3); owned by packs/vehicles): a VehicleRegistry with no planner and the personal vehicles on a recording bus. save writes no block (traversal owns extensions.traversal and does not run): {block: null}. load reads none, even a block the step states (one a file still carries): loadVehicleLayers(registry, null) (src/traversal/traversal-save.ts) puts every world vehicle back at its authored place, owner and empty, and every rider on foot, with no events. The same rule the save contract states for a save with no block (docs/village-state-save.md §8). The intent and riders steps answer the rider intent as in session.json (PL.core-ride-intent), so after such a load nobody is drawn riding.",
  "catalog": [
    "traversal-vehicles"
  ],
  "ops": [
    "run"
  ],
  "steps": {
    "run": [
      "board",
      "drive",
      "disembark",
      "mount",
      "dismount",
      "cycle",
      "save",
      "load",
      "intent",
      "riders"
    ]
  },
  "runner": "src/traversal/systems-corpus.ts (runTraversalSystemsOp). Compare exactly, object key sets included; an unknown op or step is an error.",
  "regenerate": "npm run traversal-systems-corpus; npm run traversal-systems-corpus:check fails on any difference.",
